[
    {
        "content": "<p>In PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36813\">#36813</a>, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"569722\">@Miyahara Kō</span> pointed out a structural limitation: <code>Encoding</code> currently bundles its alphabet <code>Γ</code>.</p>\n<p>To properly implement a strictly binary pair encoding, we can't use the existing <code>finEncodingPair</code> because it inflates the alphabet using a sum type (<code>ea.Γ ⊕ eb.Γ</code>). We need to explicitly specify an <code>Encoding α Bool</code>. Beyond this PR, an unbundled <code>Γ</code> is also a prerequisite for formalizing Information Theory or Coding Theory, where the alphabet's size and algebraic structure must remain fixed.<br>\n<strong>Proposal:</strong></p>\n<p>Unbundle <code>Γ</code> from the structure and make it a parameter:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Encoding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">encode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">decode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">decode_encode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">encode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>To preserve encapsulation for abstract computability proofs (where the exact alphabet doesn't matter), we can simultaneously provide a bundled fallback via a Sigma type:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AnyEncoding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">Σ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Encoding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is a breaking change for <code>Computability.Encoding</code> (e.g., <code>FinEncoding</code> will need to extend <code>Encoding α Γ</code>).</p>",
        "id": 583580031,
        "sender_full_name": "Alexey Milovanov",
        "timestamp": 1775304592
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah I don't think <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Computability.Encoding#doc\">docs#Computability.Encoding</a> is idiomatic currently. Every time it's used it should come with a specified universe <code>Encoding.{v}</code> to indicate the universe of Gamma, or else Lean might spend a long time doing universe unification. I think the proposal is a good one. It was the mathlib 3 PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib3/pull/13224\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib3/pull/13224</a> which generalised those universes; they were previously equal (in fact they were both <code>Type</code>).</p>",
        "id": 583618251,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1775343790
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"569722\">@Miyahara Kō</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"110038\">@Kevin Buzzard</span> I will go ahead and open a new PR titled <code>refactor(Computability.Encoding): unbundle Γ</code>.</p>\n<p>Just to confirm the exact implementation details before I start touching downstream files, the core changes in <code>Encoding.lean</code> will look like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- From:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Encoding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ...</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- To:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Encoding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- From:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FinEncoding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Encoding</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ΓFin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- To:</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FinEncoding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Encoding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ΓFin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And then I will mechanically update the definitions and lemmas in the rest of the files to explicitly take <code>{Γ}</code>.</p>\n<p>Does this plan look good to go?</p>",
